## Rules

- This file is written from the verbs by `__NAME__ skill`, never by hand;
  `dev build cmd/__NAME__` rewrites it and `go test` fails when it is stale.
- A verb's usage is markdown in `usage.md` beside `main.go`, and the prose
  around it is `head.md` and `tail.md`. They are files, not Go string
  constants, because a Go raw string is backtick-delimited and so can never
  hold inline code.
- Keep `usage.md` to headings, `- ` list items with two-space continuations,
  paragraphs and inline code. That is the subset the terminal rendering reads,
  and `go test` holds it there. `head.md` and `tail.md` only reach the manual,
  so they may use all of markdown.
- Write every `<placeholder>` in backticks, in all three. Unfenced, a markdown
  renderer swallows it as an HTML tag and the reader never sees it.
